From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000089 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 20:16:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini: describe DA9214 rail

The working Gemini kernel and live Device Tree identify a Dialog DA9214
at address 0x68 on MT6797 I2C6.  Live reads identify the second output as
the external Cortex-A72 Vproc rail.  The bus runs at 3.4 MHz in
push-pull mode on the existing I2C6 pin group.

Enable that bus and describe both DA9214 outputs.  Both children are required:
the upstream driver registers its regulator descriptors by array index, so a
BUCKB-only description would incorrectly register the BUCKA descriptor.

Do not add voltage limits, boot-on, always-on, or an unverified enable GPIO.
The initial diagnostic profile uses regulator_ignore_unused to preserve the
firmware state without asking the regulator core to change it.

---
 .../boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts   | 23 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
@@ -220,6 +220,29 @@ &mmc1 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&i2c6 {
+	clock-frequency = <3400000>;
+	mediatek,use-push-pull;
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	pinctrl-0 = <&i2c6_pins_a>;
+	status = "okay";
+
+	da9214: regulator@68 {
+		compatible = "dlg,da9214";
+		reg = <0x68>;
+
+		regulators {
+			da9214_bucka: BUCKA {
+				regulator-name = "da9214-bucka";
+			};
+
+			da9214_buckb: BUCKB {
+				regulator-name = "vproc-big";
+			};
+		};
+	};
+};
+
 &i2c7 {
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 	pinctrl-0 = <&i2c7_pins_a>;
-- 
2.43.0
